  "text": "In this retrospective study of patients with T4 ESCC downstaged after neo-CRT, the CRT-S group had longer OS (not available vs. 20.37 months) and PFS (21.0 vs. 8.6 months) than the D-CRT group, and treatment option was an independent predictor of PFS. Median OS in the CRT-S group was not available at data cutoff (median follow-up, 37.6 months), but our findings indicated that the 24-month OS rate was 69.4%."
